{"BrowserReportingCollector validation error response shape changed to include JSON body with 'error'/'details' fields, potentially breaking clients that relied on previous empty response body": 0.4140869677066803, "ErrorEvent is defined as a TypedDict but is being instantiated like a constructor, which is non-idiomatic and may raise TypeError depending on runtime/Python version": 0.5966222882270813, "fetch_error_details wraps TypedDict construction in try/except that silently suppresses failures and returns empty list, causing incomplete summaries and hard-to-debug missing data": 0.4901067614555359, "Feature flag 'use-table-widget-visualization' renders TableWidgetVisualization with empty columns array and empty tableData instead of actual result.data and result.meta, causing empty tables where data should be displayed": 0.9927962422370911, "BrowserReportSerializer validation for 'age'/'timestamp' uses truthiness check instead of key presence, allowing invalid reports where both fields are present if either has value 0": 0.9252703189849854, "BrowserReportingCollectorEndpoint docstring claims reports are forwarded to GCP but the code no longer forwards to any external service": 0.05762524902820587, "TabularColumn.name is typed as TFields (same as key) instead of string, incorrectly tying human-readable label type to machine field name type": 0.681419849395752, "Unsafe optional chaining in tableWidgetVisualization when extracting columnOrder - tableData?.meta.fields only chains on tableData, not meta, causing potential TypeError if tableData.meta is undefined": 0.8641371726989746, "useTraceItemAttributeKeys queryKey is derived from outer selection but queryFn uses its own internal selection from usePageFilters(), causing potential cache key mismatch and stale/incorrect caching": 0.7722460627555847}